Third-party source code linked into HackOS.  One directory per package, each
with the upstream LICENSE and an UPSTREAM file (where it came from, the exact
commit, the files taken and their hashes).  Nothing in here is edited; a local
change would have to be a recorded patch.

HackOS itself is AGPL-3.0-or-later.  Only code under licences that can be
combined with it belongs here (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0, ...).

C code never calls Adder-convention functions and Adder never calls C except
through `extern "C"` declarations; tests/check_c_link.sh enforces that at every
`make test`.  C library functions for this code come from lib/cshim, under
prefixed names (see lib/cshim/include/hackos_libc_rename.h for why).

nordic-mdk-nrf52840/ is read as data only (tests/nrf52/check_regs.py), as
nxp-mcux-rt1062/ is.  llvm-compiler-rt-builtins/ is compiled for boards
with SOFT_DOUBLE=1 only (BOARD=feather-nrf52840): it defines the run-time
ABI's __aeabi_d* helpers and calls nothing outside itself.

font8x8/ (public domain) is the glyph table of the display's text screen:
its header is compiled through drivers/display/font8x8.c into the images of
boards that have a display (the QEMU boards today) and read as data by
tests/display/panel2png.py.
